From 747bbb461cab62979e67380ae9a78b370e335ca2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:06:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: no SLP/ALP token index on Lotus V2 nodes

SLP/ALP token indexing is off on Lotus V2 nodes (user decision
2026-10-19). The native Chronik already follows it (HostCapabilities
slp_alp_tokens is false on V2 nodes), but the Rust Chronik still indexed
tokens on V2, so the two disagreed on every token-carrying response
(validate-tx, /tx, script history).

On a node whose outputs have V2 fields, -chroniktokenindex now defaults
to 0, and -chroniktokenindex=1 is an init error that names the option and
the reason. An existing token index is wiped on the next start, as for
an explicit -chroniktokenindex=0. eCash nodes keep the token index on by
default.

Tests: a "chronik_token_index" requirement skips, with the stated reason,
the SLP/ALP-only functional tests: chronik_token_alp, _broadcast_txs,
_burn, _id_group, _parse_failure, _script_group, _slp_fungible,
_slp_mint_vault, _slp_nft1, chronik_script_batch_summary and
chronik_disable_token_index. chronik_lokad_id_group no longer enables
the token index on its reindex restart.

Tier: V2 (fixup to "v2: swap chronik-bridge and chronik-cpp to V2 headers
and outputs"; test skips: "test(v2): migrate functional fixtures and
harnesses to native transactions")
